tasks/dsh-parity\waves\RESULT-W7.md:10:- **E14 — PARTIAL.** The current branch already has per-call Docker behavior in `core/atlas/sandbox.py`: `read-only` runs in a disposable container with a read-only workspace bind mount; `workspace-write` runs in the run container; each result reports `sandbox_permissions` and `sandbox_enforced`; `danger-full-access` is rejected with `sandbox_enforced: false`. New W7 tests cover these command boundaries and reporting. The Windows host executor still has no general per-call OS isolation implementation. Docker CLI was present, but Docker Engine was unavailable (`Server: null`, Docker Desktop Linux pipe missing), so Docker execution itself was not exercised on this machine.
tasks/dsh-parity\waves\RESULT-W7.md:11:- **E18 — PARTIAL.** The current branch already validates `sandbox_permissions` and non-empty `justification`, sends one approval request marked `_approval_no_always`, and routes the accepted mode only to the current Docker call. An unavailable executor fails closed. The focused unit tests pass, but a real model call did not reach tool/approval execution; live end-to-end UI approval and tool dispatch remain unobserved.
