tasks/dsh-parity\waves\logs\W16.log:2564:docs\engine\GAPS.md:27:**Intentionally retained / not ported.** Streamed reasoning and tool fragments stay internal and are not exposed as new wire events; partial persistence remains limited to assistant text/refusal, with reasoning/tool fragments represented in repair telemetry. Atlas keeps its existing session database, tool scheduler, model transport, event dictionaries and bounded turn limit rather than adopting Codex/ZCode runtime types. PreToolUse `defer` returns a denied tool result because Atlas has no durable suspend/resume approval protocol. The loop consumes SessionStart `additional_context`; other normalized hook metadata such as watch paths or reload-skills is not given new runtime side effects here. If PreCompact blocks, compaction is skipped; a provider overflow can therefore still fail because the same oversized context must be retried. Durable background task controls and provider-specific transport/session mechanisms remain at their existing Atlas owners.
