tasks/dsh-parity\waves\logs\W5.log:327:scope: Read-only inventory and risk-ranked cleanup of C/D/E, plus explicitly authorized software or directory removal. Use for Windows storage-recovery requests; distinguishes caches from personal, project, model, game, and Docker data.
tasks/dsh-parity\waves\logs\W5.log:348:- C-D-E drives, Get-Volume, ComfyUI, D:\comfy, MuMuPlayer, uninstall.exe, MuMuRemoteService, DockerData, docker_data.vhdx, $RECYCLE.BIN, Remove-Item, execution-policy
tasks/dsh-parity\waves\logs\W5.log:352:- when asking “扫描全电脑，告诉我那些都可以删掉”, the user accepted a read-only, risk-ranked inventory before deletion -> separate “可直接删”, “需确认”, and “不建议删”; never classify personal data, projects, games, models, or Docker storage as junk merely by path. [Task 1][Task 2]
tasks/dsh-parity\waves\logs\W5.log:359:- High-value candidates require context: `E:\$RECYCLE.BIN` is reclaimable only after confirming recovery is not needed; `C:\Users\25011\AppData\Local\Temp` included active Huya cache; `E:\DockerData\disk\docker_data.vhdx` must not be deleted directly, especially while Docker is unavailable. [Task 2]
tasks/dsh-parity\waves\logs\W5.log:1268:- Atlas exposes `run.start`, `resume(after_sequence)`, `run.cancel`, `run.pause`, `run.resume`, `approval.response`, events, reconnect/replay, and workflow journal primitives. Static evidence indicates ZCode 3.15.1 has broader workflow UI exposure for phases, artifacts, questions, runtime retune, and per-run settings; Atlas has no confirmed equivalent main-chat UI for runtime retune or per-node model choice. [Task 2]
tasks/dsh-parity\waves\logs\W5.log:1269:- A valid parity result needs same provider/model or an explicit model-difference boundary plus controlled scenarios: chat, file read/write, terminal, browser, approval, stop, pause/resume, reconnect, workflow concurrency retune, artifact view, and rerun. `/api/health` ready, a changelog, or static source cannot substitute. [Task 2]
